From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wiaaut: WIA Automation, the scripting objects of image acquisition (8302)

wiaaut: WIA Automation, the scripting objects of image acquisition

Wine had no wiaaut.dll, so scripts (VBScript, PowerShell) and .NET programs
using WIA through it -- Paint.NET's "From Scanner or Camera" -- found nothing.
The type library and the objects are those of Windows' WIA Automation Library
v2.0, with its class, interface and dispatch IDs: WIA.DeviceManager (DeviceInfos,
persistent event handlers), DeviceInfo/Device/Item with Items, Commands, Events,
Formats and Properties (by name or number; value, type, read-only, range or list),
Item.Transfer into an ImageFile (format, extension, size, resolution, depth,
FileData, ARGBData, LoadFile, SaveFile that does not replace a file),
WIA.ImageProcess with the RotateFlip, Crop, Scale and Convert filters,
WIA.Vector (values, BinaryData, String, Date, Picture), WIA.Rational, and
WIA.CommonDialog: ShowAcquireImage, ShowSelectDevice, ShowSelectItems,
ShowTransfer, ShowDeviceProperties/ShowItemProperties and ShowAcquisitionWizard
through the WIA dialogs, a cancelled dialog an error (0x80210064) only with
CancelError. Everything goes through the WIA service.
